# Supabase Configuration for DevChat Local
# ==========================================
# These environment variables enable cloud sync and OAuth authentication

# Your Supabase Project URL (already configured)
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL=https://cgwmhcmioxxteajbtsdd.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://cgwmhcmioxxteajbtsdd.supabase.co

# Your Supabase Anon/Public Key (get from Supabase Dashboard)
# Go to: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/cgwmhcmioxxteajbtsdd/settings/api
# Copy the "anon public" key and paste it below
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_DEFAULT_KEY=your-anon-key-here
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# 📖 OAuth Setup Instructions:
# =============================
# 
# To enable GitHub and Google login:
# 1. Go to your Supabase Dashboard > Authentication > Providers
# 2. Enable GitHub Provider:
#    - Go to https://github.com/settings/developers
#    - Create new OAuth App with callback: https://cgwmhcmioxxteajbtsdd.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#    - Copy Client ID and Secret to Supabase
# 3. Enable Google Provider:
#    - Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    - Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID with redirect URI: https://cgwmhcmioxxteajbtsdd.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#    - Copy Client ID and Secret to Supabase
#
# 📚 For detailed setup, see:
# - QUICK_SETUP.md - Quick start guide
# - SUPABASE_SETUP.md - Detailed Supabase configuration
# - backend/README.md - Optional FastAPI backend (advanced users)
#
# ⚠️ Security Notes:
# - Use the "anon public" key (safe for client-side)
# - NEVER use the "service_role" key here!
# - Don't commit your actual .env file to git
# - Configure Site URL in Supabase: https://your-domain.com
